From 182d8e92bec753b8eed6b6a8655a9bbfbd3900ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jonaslacour <jonaslacour1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:08:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Metal] Keep translation time linear in the size of large
 unrolled kernels

A fully unrolled kernel with many wide joins (BatchLAS's register-resident
posv at order 28-32: ~1300 blocks, ~6400 PHIs) spent minutes in the Metal
translator, in three places:

- StructurizeCFG repairs every PHI it reroutes with its own SSAUpdater,
  whose FindExistingPHI scans every PHI of every block it walks. The PHIs
  are now demoted to stack slots first (DemotePHIToStack, no critical-edge
  splitting) and PromotePass rebuilds SSA on the structured CFG.
- MetalEmitter::valueName and the IR comments called printAsOperand/print
  without a ModuleSlotTracker, which renumbers the whole function for every
  unnamed value. A per-function tracker and a name cache replace that.
- Value names grown by SROA/unroll suffixes (hundreds of characters) were
  copied into the MSL verbatim. Local names over 48 characters are cut and
  every local name is made unique after sanitizing. The IR comments are now
  emitted only with __ACPP_PRINT_METAL_CODE or __ACPP_METAL_IR_COMMENTS.

posv float N=32 NC=28 NR=1: 90 s -> 1.3 s to translate, 3.5 MB -> 7.1 MB of
MSL without comments (the old figure included them).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EPytkCH8xVwQyJeGegbGzF
